. The 2s may be one shape or several.\n\n**What the outputs show.**\n- **Pair 1:** the little 2‑shape above‑left of the 3‑block reappears three more times:\n  - mirrored left↔right to the upper right,\n  - mirrored up↔down to the lower left,\n  - mirrored both ways to the lower right.\n\n  The four copies are placed symmetrically around the 3‑block.\n- **Pair 2:** the same thing happens with the \"U\" shape.\n- **Pair 3:** the input already has all four mirrored quadrants. The fact sheet says it is symmetric with x ↦ 11−x and y ↦ 9−y. The 3‑block spans x 5..6, so 5+6 = 11, and y 4..5, so 4+5 = 9. The mirror axes therefore run exactly through the centre of the 3‑block, which is why the output equals the input.\n\n**Rule.** Let the 3‑block's bounding box be (y0, x0, y1, x1). Make the colour‑2 pattern symmetric under:\n- x ↦ x0+x1−x,\n- y ↦ y0+y1−y,\n- and both together.\n\nCopying every 2 cell to its partners leaves existing cells unchanged. That explains why pair 3 stays identical.\n\n**Checks against the demonstrations.**\n- **Pair 1:** the 3‑block is at rows 3–4 and cols 4–5, so cells reflect with y ↦ 7−y and x ↦ 9−x. The 2 at (0,1) goes to (0,8), (7,1) and (7,8), all of which are listed as added cells.\n- **Pair 2:** the 3‑block is at rows 7–8 and cols 9–10, so the maps are y ↦ 15−y and x ↦ 19−x. The U at cols 5–8 maps to cols 11–14, and rows 3–6 map to rows 9–12, matching the output.\n\n**Test input.** The 3‑block is at rows 6–7 and cols 6–7, so the maps are y ↦ 13−y and x ↦ 13−x.\n- The 2‑shape occupies rows 2–5 and cols 2–5.\n- The mirrored copies land in cols 8–11 and rows 8–11, which fit inside the 18×14 grid.\n- To be safe, the program skips any partner cell that would fall outside the grid.\n\n**Construction stages.**\n1. Start from the input.\n2. Add the left‑right mirror images of the 2s.\n3. Add the up‑down mirror images of everything so far, which also produces the diagonal copy.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid).copy()\n    H, W = g.shape\n    bg = background(g)\n    ys, xs = np.where(g == 3)\n    sy = ys.min() + ys.max()\n    sx = xs.min() + xs.max()\n    # colour(s) of the pattern to mirror: everything except bg and the 3-block\n    pat_cols = [c for c in np.unique(g) if c != bg and c != 3]\n\n    # Stage 1: mirror left<->right across the vertical axis through the 3-block centre\n    out = g.copy()\n    for y, x in zip(*np.where(np.isin(g, pat_cols))):\n        nx = sx - x\n        if 0 <= nx < W and out[y, nx] == bg:\n            out[y, nx] = g[y, x]\n    emit(out.copy(), \"Mirror the colour-2 pattern left-right across the vertical axis through the centre of the 3 block.\")\n\n    # Stage 2: mirror up<->down across the horizontal axis through the 3-block centre\n    cur = out.copy()\n    for y, x in zip(*np.where(np.isin(cur, pat_cols))):\n        ny = sy - y\n        if 0 <= ny < H and out[ny, x] == bg:\n            out[ny, x] = cur[y, x]\n    emit(out.copy(), \"Mirror everything up-down across the horizontal axis through the 3 block, completing all four quadrants.\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"rigid":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"- mirrored left↔right to the upper right,"},{"source":"final explanation","text":"- mirrored up↔down to the lower left,"},{"source":"final explanation","text":"- mirrored both ways to the lower right."}],"dynamics":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"- To be safe, the program skips any partner cell that would fall outside the grid."}],"crop":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"**Rule.** Let the 3‑block's bounding box be (y0, x0, y1, x1)."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"b757889b2be2f387b9524b0f80982f0deb32a27132059e2ceb7ce7d22bd960cf","task_sha256":"444ee3e0877998ce306f8b0d277c43b1b3cef4551a9d91c2e80f156b747fd08a","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
